.TH JARVIS 1 "May 2026" "Jarvis CLI 0.8.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jarvis \- personal AI assistant CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jarvis
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIargs\fR] [\fI\-\-flags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jarvis
is a native C binary that controls the Jarvis AI platform.
It reads
.I state.json
offline and communicates with a FastAPI server (default
.IR http://127.0.0.1:5050 )
online.
Online commands fall back gracefully when the API is unreachable.
.SH CORE COMMANDS
.TP
.B jarvis
Show the default landing screen (date, system, tip).
.TP
.B jarvis help
Print the full command reference.
.TP
.B jarvis version
Show version, compiler, OS, and build date.
.TP
.B jarvis config
Display all current config values (from
.I ~/.jarvis/config
plus compiled defaults). The
.I api_key
is masked to the first 8 characters.
.TP
.B jarvis time
Show current date, clock, and timezone.
.TP
.B jarvis hello
Greeting with version and timestamp.
.SH OFFLINE COMMANDS
Read
.I state.json
directly \[em] no API required.
.TP
.B jarvis who
Identity profile: name, role, domain, host, ID.
.TP
.B jarvis focus
Current focus and next actions from the workflow.
.TP
.B jarvis tasks [\fI\-\-blocked\fR]
Task list with status icons.
.B \-\-blocked
shows only blocked tasks and expands each task's blockers array.
.TP
.B jarvis memory [\fIsearch\fR \fIquery\fR] [\fItag\fR \fItype\fR]
Recent memory entries (last 10).
.B search
\fIquery\fR performs a case-insensitive substring search across all entries.
.B tag
\fItype\fR filters to entries whose
.I type
field exactly matches (e.g.
.BR note ,
.BR decision ).
.TP
.B jarvis add-task \fItitle\fR
Append a new task to the workflow (auto-assigns ID: task-001, task-002, ...).
Writes directly to
.I state.json
via Python.
.TP
.B jarvis done \fItask-id\fR
Mark a task done by ID (e.g.
.IR task-003 ).
.TP
.B jarvis estimate \fItask-id\fR \fIminutes\fR
Set the time estimate for a task.
The estimate appears in
.B jarvis tasks
output alongside the task, and a total remaining estimate is shown at the bottom.
.SH ONLINE COMMANDS
Require the API server.
Auto-detect: pings
.I /api/health
with a 2-second timeout.
.TP
.B jarvis status
Live platform overview: focus, tasks, device, workflow state.
Falls back to offline state if API is unreachable.
.TP
.B jarvis health
Platform health check: API server, network, device status.
.TP
.B jarvis run \fIcommand\fR
POST a raw command string to
.I /api/command
and print the result.
.TP
.B jarvis ask [\fI\-\-stream\fR] [\fI\-\-model\fR \fImodel\fR] \fIquestion\fR
Ask the AI a question.
Routes: API server first, then Ollama at
.I ai_url
(\fI/api/generate\fR).
.B \-\-stream
skips the API and streams tokens directly from Ollama as they arrive.
.B \-\-model
overrides
.I ai_model
for this call only.
.TP
.B jarvis remember \fInote\fR
Save a memory note via the API.
.TP
.B jarvis set-focus \fItext\fR
Update the current focus via the API.
.TP
.B jarvis sync
Display sync manifest, peer list, and state summary.
.TP
.B jarvis journal [\fIhours\fR]
Recent activity feed. Default: last 6 hours.
.SH WORKSPACE
.TP
.B jarvis projects
Scan
.I projects_root
for git repositories and display a table: name, branch, dirty flag, latest commit.
.SH LIVE
.TP
.B jarvis watch [\fItarget\fR] [\fI-n secs\fR]
Live-refresh any view. Default target:
.IR status .
Default interval: 10 seconds.
Press Ctrl-C to exit cleanly.
.TP
.B jarvis daemon \fIstart\fR|\fIstop\fR|\fIstatus\fR
Background poller. Polls
.I /api/live
every 30 seconds; sends a desktop notification on focus changes and task completions.
PID file:
.IR ~/.jarvis/daemon.pid .
Log:
.IR ~/.jarvis/daemon.log .
.TP
.B jarvis notify \fImessage\fR
Send a desktop notification via
.BR notify-send (1).
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable ANSI colour output.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Raw JSON output (future phases).
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I ~/.jarvis/config
\[em] KEY=VALUE pairs, one per line.
.PP
.TS
l l.
Key	Default
api_url	http://127.0.0.1:5050
api_key	(empty)
name	Amit
ai_provider	ollama
ai_model	llama3.2
ai_url	http://127.0.0.1:11434
state_path	dev/projects/work_station/Kingofyadav/state.json
projects_root	(empty)
no_color	0
.TE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.jarvis/config
Runtime configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.jarvis/daemon.pid
PID of the running background daemon.
.TP
.I ~/.jarvis/daemon.log
Daemon activity log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR notify-send (1),
.BR ollama (1),
.BR curl (1)
